    description: "INV-nular member, found 2026-09-06 while sizing the javascript completeness leg: PURE PATH ARITHMETIC ROWED AS A FILESYSTEM READ. Swept by mechanism across all fifteen catalogues (load_catalog, names in {join, basename, dirname, extname, normalize, relative, resolve, abspath, normpath, split, ...} under fs_*):\n\n  javascript  path.basename, path.dirname, path.extname, path.join, path.normalize, path.relative, path.resolve   fs_read   7 rows\n  python      os.path.abspath, posixpath.abspath                                                                  fs_read   2 rows\n  NOT members, checked and kept: pathlib.Path.resolve (follows symlinks -- a real fs read), xml.etree.ElementTree.parse (reads a file), go filepath.Walk/WalkDir/Glob (traverse the fs).\n\nWHY IT IS A KIND ERROR AND NOT A NIT. path.join and friends touch no file: they are string operations (path.resolve and abspath read process.cwd() / os.getcwd(), a host_info_read at most, and read nothing about the path they return). fs_read mints no taint, so the cost is not a false taint flow; it is (1) io-boundaries reporting a filesystem-read chain at every path.join in a repository, and (2) INV-buzab's gate: a CLASSIFIED call counts as EXAMINED, so a program whose only \"I/O\" is path arithmetic classifies as a program with filesystem reads and can never be told apart from one. The 08-28 sweep's strata (constructors, handle names, lifecycle callbacks, adjacency) did not include \"string helper on a path-shaped name\", which is a fifth syntactic proxy the root cause predicts and the sweep did not run.\n\nTHE FIX IS DELETION WITH A NOTE at the deletion site (F1/F2's pattern, #602), then the javascript `path` module becomes a COMPLETE module_completeness grant with zero rows -- which is exactly the entry the javascript leg (the sibling item filed the same day) must author, so land the two together or this first. A/B on the javascript and python corpus repos: fs_read chain counts and every verdict that changes category read back; the removal direction is live (`removed>0`), so every removed chain is listed."  # 4da6
